  ('shiga-kogen-japan', '08A', 'Shiga Kogen', 'Japan', 'Japan''s biggest linked ski area, dry high-altitude powder into', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Japanese Alps/Nagano', '{"ski","adventure","wildlife","wellness","family","culinary","culture","hiking"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Japan''s largest interconnected ski area: ~18 resorts on one all-area pass (some say 19; ~5 macro-areas), ~48 lifts, ~80 km runs / ~600 ha / ~81 courses","Mt Yokote (Yokoteyama) ~2,307 m = Japan''s highest lift-served run; whole-area vertical ~982 m from 1,325 m base; inside Joshin''etsu-kogen National Park + 1980 UNESCO MAB reserve","Dry high-altitude powder ~12 m a season; one of Japan''s longest seasons (late Nov into mid-May incl Golden Week on high peaks)","1998 Nagano Olympic venue (slalom/snowboard on Yakebitaiyama; giant slalom in complex - verify exact peak); Jigokudani snow monkeys ~30 min away","All-area adult pass 2025-26: 1-day JPY 9,000 / 2-day 17,500 / 3-day 26,000 / 6-day 51,500; child 1-day 4,100; free-child Ski Kids'' Day Sundays; night skiing across 5 areas","Top stays: Okushiga Kogen Hotel (premier-luxury, indoor onsen + French/Japanese dining) + Shiga Kogen Prince Hotel (ski-in/out); LUXURY/ULTRA TIER THIN, no private-chalet market","Access ~90-110 min Tokyo-Nagano Shinkansen + ~70-90 min bus; Nagano-city Zenkoji Temple + Obuse cultural day-trips","Backcountry is GUIDED-ONLY (registered tours; gate-accessed tree runs + Yokoteyama touring); NO dedicated JAN daily bulletin"],"safety":{"emergency":"110 police / 119 fire + ambulance / #7119 medical advice / 118 coast guard; JNTO Japan Visitor Hotline 050-3816-2787 (multilingual 24-hr); ambulance dispatch free","hospital":"Nagano Red Cross Hospital (Nagano City, nearest large hospital) via 119; Shinshu University Hospital (Matsumoto) for higher-level trauma; JNTO Nagano medical list (English)","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","acti