  ('ambergris-caye-belize', '10S', 'Ambergris Caye / San Pedro', 'Belize', 'Ambergris Caye Belize', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Belize', '{"tropical","liveaboard","romance","expedition"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Belize''s largest island and #1 tourism engine; runs parallel to the UNESCO Belize Barrier Reef, ~35 mi NE of Belize City.","Hol Chan Marine Reserve (est. 1987, ~4 mi south of San Pedro) protects ~18 km2 with 160+ fish species; Shark Ray Alley added 1999.","Belize''s national recompression capability is on-island: SSS hyperbaric chamber (since 1989) + DAN-affiliated Belize Chamber Project (2015), both 24/7.","Air access via BZE Philip Goldson Intl -> SPR San Pedro, ~20-min puddle-jumper (Tropic Air / Maya Island Air) or ~90-min water taxi via Caye Caulker.","English is Belize''s official language - the only English-official nation in Central America."],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (also 90); San Pedro Police 206-2022; San Pedro Coast Guard 222-5260","hyperbaric_chamber":"YES - on Ambergris/San Pedro: SSS Belize Hyperbaric Facility (est. 1989, 4-diver lock, US Navy tables, 24/7) + DAN-affiliated Belize Chamber Project (2015). National dive-safety asset.","hospital":"Lighthouse Medical Center (San Pedro, private) for urgent care; serious trauma -> Karl Heusner Memorial Hospital (KHMH), Belize City - the only trauma centre in Belize; then US evac. Island remoteness flagged.","book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":true,"malaria":"none on the cayes; Belize WHO-certified malaria-free 2023; small mainland Cayo District cluster (Apr 2025) - mainland only","water":"do not drink tap water on the cayes; use bottled/filtered","mosquito_borne":"dengue primary concern; also chikungunya, Zika (day-biting Aedes) - use repellent","founder_policy_note":"only Southside Belize City is the named danger","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://ww